To generate an automatic table of contents (TOC) in a LaTeX document, you can use the following commands:

1. Add the `toc` option to the `\documentclass` command, as shown below:

   ```
   \documentclass[toc]{article}
   ```

   Or for a book:

   ```
   \documentclass[toc]{book}
   ```

2. Add the `\tableofcontents` command at the beginning of your document, after the `\begin{document}` command:

   ```
   \begin{document}
     \tableofcontents
     ...
   \end{document}
   ```

3. Add the `\label` command before each section or chapter heading:

   ```
   \section{Section 1}\label{sec:section1}
   ```

   Or for a chapter:

   ```
   \chapter{Chapter 1}\label{chap:chapter1}
   ```

4. Add the `\addcontentsline` command to manually add section/chapter titles to the TOC, if necessary:

   ```
   \section{Unnumbered Section}\label{sec:unnumbered}
   \addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Unnumbered Section}\label{sec:unnumbered-toc}
   ```

   Note: The first argument (`toc`) specifies the file to write to (in this case, the TOC); the second argument specifies the sectioning level (e.g., `section`, `subsection`, `subsubsection`, etc.); and the third argument specifies the text to display in the TOC.

5. Compile your document twice (or more, depending on your document complexity) to generate the TOC.

Here's a complete example:

```latex
\documentclass[toc]{article}

\begin{document}
  \tableofcontents

  \section{Section 1}\label{sec:section1}
  \subsection{Subsection 1.1}\label{sec:subsec11}
  \subsection{Subsection 1.2}\label{sec:subsec12}

  \section{Section 2}\label{sec:section2}

  \chapter{Chapter 1}\label{chap:chapter1}
  \section{Section 3}\label{sec:section3}

  \section{Unnumbered Section}\label{sec:unnumbered}
  \addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Unnumbered Section}\label{sec:unnumbered-toc}

  \appendix
  \chapter{Appendix 1}\label{chap:appendix1}
  \section{Section A1}\label{sec:appendix1}

\end{document}
```

When compiled, the resulting TOC will look like:

```
Contents
--------
1. Section 1 4
   1.1 Subsection 1.1 5
   1.2 Subsection 1.2 5
2. Section 2 6
3. Chapter 1 7
   3.1 Section 3 8
4. Unnumbered Section 9
Appendices
---------
A. Appendix 1 10
   A.1 Section A1 11
``` 

Note that the page numbers may differ depending on the content of your document. Also, the TOC will be updated automatically as you add, remove, or modify section/chapter headings.

